.TH ACCESSWHY 1
.SH NAME
accesswhy \\- explain local mode-bit access evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B accesswhy
accesswhy --path PATH [--format json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Emits JSON mode-bit and current-identity evidence, and explicitly reports unavailable ACL, mount, and LSM evidence.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBaccesswhy --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
